WEBVTT

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:13.100
Good morning, Alice.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:15.840
Sprinkling water on the walk, huh?

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:19.190
Shino! I hope you're faring
well in the summer heat.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.080
I hope you're well, too.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:29.070
<i>My second summer vacation since coming
to Japan is just around the corner.</i>

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:32.960
Swift as Wind
Silent as Forest
Fierce as Fire
Immovable as Mountain

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:08.260
Episode 8
Almost Summer Vacation

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:10.100
I want to plan out my
summer vacation this year!

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:14.350
Last year, I didn't do everything
I wanted to, so it felt incomplete!

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:18.310
We had fun hiking and going to the festival.

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:21.110
There's a lot more to
enjoy during the summer!

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:24.860
This year, I want to play with all
my might until I'm burned out!

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:27.110
Actually, I want to burn out!

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:28.860
Hey, calm down.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:32.330
I'm an unstoppable runaway train right now!

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:34.870
Where'd you leave your brakes?!

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:39.710
Well, it's true that planning ahead is important.

00:02:39.710 --> 00:02:41.840
Where do you want to go, Youko?

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:43.130
Well, naturally...

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:44.380
The beach!

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:44.380
The sky!

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:48.540
Is this a repeat of last year?!

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:51.280
What does "sky" even mean?!

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:52.760
Skydiving, maybe?

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:53.680
Beach!

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:54.640
Sky!

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:55.550
Beach!

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:56.430
Sky!

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:59.640
This year, we're going to the beach!

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:01.830
I want to go to the sky!

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:03.750
They're so passionate.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.070
They sure are.

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:08.200
C'mon, let's go to the beach this year.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:10.110
I want to go to the beach!

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:12.120
Beach, beach, beach!

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:12.120
Oh, all right.

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:14.850
Okay. We can go to the beach this year.

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:15.950
All right!

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:17.520
Beach!

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:19.300
The beach, huh?

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.650
Shino, don't you like the beach?

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:25.210
Well, you see, I was once
attacked by a gang from the sea.

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:27.210
You mean killer whales?!

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:28.250
No.

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:31.400
It was a hermit crab.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:34.440
Shinobu!

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:35.260
That's so cute!

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:37.520
Hermit crabs are cute.

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:40.120
But Onee-chan told me they were dangerous.

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:41.830
It'll be fine.

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:43.790
I can't wait to go to the beach.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:46.130
Oh, I don't have a swimsuit.

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:47.280
<i>The beach, huh?</i>

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:49.200
<i>I don't like that idea.</i>

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.390
<i>I'm no good at swimming,</i>

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:53.490
<i>but even worse at wearing a swimsuit...</i>

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:54.740
Sigh

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:58.250
Aya, you don't have a swimsuit, either?

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:01.390
I don't have the waist (kubire)
for one... or the chest...

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:02.420
Um...

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:06.000
<i>What fin (hire) is "kubire"?</i>

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:10.500
Wh-What...

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:11.980
You've got a waist!

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:15.570
Oh, right. "Kubire" means waist.

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:19.070
It's okay. You've got a nice waist, Aya.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:22.010
Yeah! You should be more confident!

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:26.230
She's crying!

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:27.020
Sorry!

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:30.100
Aya...

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:33.730
I really am sorry for making you feel—

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:39.620
Hey, stop!

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:45.150
<i>Ayaya's as scary as my mom
when she gets angry.</i>

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:46.550
<i>I'd better be careful.</i>

00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:49.250
Honestly...

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:51.880
Pant         Pant         Pant

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:51.880
You guys are getting too excited.

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:54.550
Before thinking about summer vacation,

00:04:54.550 --> 00:04:57.380
shouldn't you be worrying
about next week's final ex—

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:01.140
Th-That bad?!

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:08.420
Alice. Youko-chan.

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:09.650
Let's go home.

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:11.410
We came to get you!

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:12.700
Okay.

00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:14.910
What happened, Youko?

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.620
Since when do you have bad eyesight?

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:18.910
Oh, these?

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:21.200
You weren't wearing them this morning.

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:23.880
Do you only wear them during class?

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:27.410
No, no, they're for our tests.

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:29.420
Don't I look smarter in glasses?

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:31.070
Let's see...

00:05:32.090 --> 00:05:33.690
A deviation value of about 100?

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:36.300
That's odd. You look stupid to me.

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:37.310
What?

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:41.040
Then, can I ask you some
questions about the test?

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:43.440
I'd like some help, too!

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:44.910
Sure, I don't mind...

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:49.060
In that case, let's stop
somewhere on the way home.

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:53.220
I know! Why don't we have
something to eat while we study?

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:54.560
I agree.

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:55.840
Me, too.

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:57.820
You don't seem motivated to study at all!

00:05:58.150 --> 00:06:00.580
I'm totally motivated!

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:03.010
These glasses aren't just for show...

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:08.330
Vision 2.0

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:05.250
They're prescription lenses!

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:06.450
<i>She's an idiot!</i>

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:08.330
I feel dizzy!

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:11.590
A hamburger place!

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:17.840
Coming here on the way home makes me
feel like a real high school student.

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:19.320
Let's go in.

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:24.120
Are you—

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:26.060
Sorry, Grandma.

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:29.880
G-Grandma?

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:31.240
Grandma, over here!

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:32.540
Okay, okay.

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:33.100
Grandma...

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:35.570
Shino, get it together!

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:35.860
Grandma...

00:06:35.570 --> 00:06:37.380
It was an honest mistake!

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:44.340
But I'm a young and spry
high school second year...

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:46.360
<i>Just saying that makes you sound old!</i>

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:47.940
Thanks for waiting.

00:06:48.770 --> 00:06:51.130
Why don't you guys order something, too?

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:51.850
Okay.

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:54.670
What would you like?

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:56.330
Well...

00:06:56.330 --> 00:07:00.330
Oh, yeah, this is Alice's first time
eating fast food in Japan.

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:01.610
It is?

00:07:01.610 --> 00:07:02.950
It's okay.

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:06.680
I've had fast food in England,
and this is my second year in Japan.

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:13.120
<i>Then again, maybe they order differently
here than we do in England.</i>

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:16.100
<i>I'll watch what Karen does.</i>

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:18.060
Enjoy your meal.

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:20.450
Um...

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:23.460
I'd like a chicken burger, a cola, and...

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:26.880
And one smile, please.

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:29.960
Intentional

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:31.300
<i>A smile?</i>

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:34.880
<i>But maybe this is normal in Japan.</i>

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:39.080
Next customer, please.

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:40.280
O-Okay.

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:45.030
Welcome. What would you like?

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:48.730
Um, a cheeseburger meal, and...

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:50.710
One smile, please!

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:50.270
Serious

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:54.110
Huh? What is it, Shino?

00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:56.150
Alice, that's so cute.

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:58.980
<i>Shino's laughing at me?</i>

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:02.530
You're so mean, Karen!

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:04.410
Sorry.

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:09.900
What's wrong, Karen?

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:12.920
I'd like to try working at a place like this!

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:15.380
You'd probably stand out.

00:08:15.380 --> 00:08:18.850
And I've got a big voice.

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:22.570
Karen, wait!

00:08:23.450 --> 00:08:25.740
Don't shout inside the store.

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:28.020
I was just going to say "welcome."

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:28.880
No.

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:29.740
How about quietly?

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:31.810
No. You'll summon the Namahage!

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:34.560
Any bad kids around here?!

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:38.530
So scary...

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:39.960
<i>That actually worked?</i>

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:46.050
What kind of job would you like to try, Alice?

00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:51.290
I'd like to do something I can only do in Japan.

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:53.690
Like sorting New Year's cards.

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:55.670
I think your knowledge is a little biased.

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:58.140
Only in Japan, huh?

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:00.210
A shrine maiden would be really nice.

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:02.720
Shino would look great as one.

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:03.380
What?

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:06.940
I bet all the fortunes Shino handed
out would bring good luck.

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:09.810
You're both flattering me.

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:14.470
I'm not sure that look would
suit this Western face.

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:15.810
Whose Western face?

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:22.610
What are you doing? You're so clumsy.

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:24.320
What should I do?

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:28.010
<i>I wish I could experience a
restaurant situation like that...</i>

00:09:24.820 --> 00:09:26.710
You're hopeless.

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:28.310
Thanks.

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:34.210
What are you doing? You're so clumsy.

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:36.570
Th-Thanks...

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:38.140
You're hopeless.

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:39.250
<i>How wonderful!</i>

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:41.570
<i>Even if it's with Youko, for some reason!</i>

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:45.380
<i>The problem is my clothes will get dirty,</i>

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:46.470
<i>but...</i>

00:09:46.470 --> 00:09:48.930
Some sacrifices have to be made!

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:53.480
Rumble

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:51.170
What's wrong, Aya?!

00:09:51.170 --> 00:09:53.480
Is something bothering you?

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:57.280
I'm so full...

00:09:57.590 --> 00:09:59.190
What will we do, Shino?

00:09:59.190 --> 00:10:01.960
We won't have room for dinner at home now.

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:03.240
You're right.

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:06.430
You guys didn't call home first?

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:09.280
It's inconvenient not to have a
cell phone at times like these.

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:11.590
You can use mine.

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:12.640
Here.

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:14.300
Thanks.

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:15.750
I'll make the call.

00:10:18.570 --> 00:10:20.750
<i>Is this really a cell phone?</i>

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:23.750
Are you teasing me again?

00:10:23.750 --> 00:10:25.920
I'm not teasing you.

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:28.130
I'll show you how to use it.

00:10:28.130 --> 00:10:29.510
Really?

00:10:29.510 --> 00:10:32.330
Push this, and then this.

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:33.810
O-Okay.

00:10:33.810 --> 00:10:36.120
Then, you make your selection from here.

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:36.900
Here?

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:38.180
Yeah.

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:42.650
Alice looks like she's gotten a little taller.

00:10:42.920 --> 00:10:44.300
You think so?

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:48.210
She doesn't look that different to me.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.540
Thanks for waiting.

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.660
We successfully completed the call.

00:10:54.070 --> 00:10:55.790
What were you talking about?

00:10:55.790 --> 00:10:57.900
About you looking taller.

00:10:57.900 --> 00:10:59.530
Huh? Really?

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:01.420
I thought you did,

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:03.510
but it was just my imagination.

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:04.920
That joy was short-lived!

00:11:05.170 --> 00:11:07.520
But your mind has grown!

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:09.510
It's hard to notice since I see you every day,

00:11:09.510 --> 00:11:11.930
but I'm sure other people
would hardly recognize you!

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:14.790
Your parents would be shocked

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:16.680
if they saw you now.

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:21.000
Come to think of it, you haven't been
back to England in over a year, have you?

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:24.150
Nope. I talk to them on the phone, though.

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:26.190
Don't you miss your parents?

00:11:26.690 --> 00:11:28.870
I do, but Shino...

00:11:29.550 --> 00:11:30.950
Shino...

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:33.250
Shino!

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:34.700
<i>It's my fault?!</i>

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:37.220
England is far away.

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:40.210
I don't want to leave Shino.

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:41.770
Alice...

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:48.580
I think you should go home for a visit.

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:52.580
What? You won't be lonely without me?

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:54.220
Of course I'll miss you.

00:11:54.690 --> 00:12:02.040
But I'd like your parents to see how much
you've grown since you came to Japan.

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:07.760
I'm going to England with
my family this summer.

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:09.750
Why don't you go with us?

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:10.830
With you?

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:12.070
What a great idea.

00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:17.080
You're right.

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:19.350
Just for a few days, then.

00:12:19.350 --> 00:12:20.330
Then it's settled!

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:22.730
Sounds exciting.

00:12:22.730 --> 00:12:24.640
I wonder how they're doing.

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:26.220
Bring back souvenirs for us.

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:27.020
Okay.

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:33.060
Go show your parents how well you're doing!

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:34.340
You're making it hard for her to go!

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:36.960
Come with me, Shino!

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:40.350
No, I couldn't intrude on your family time.

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:43.590
I really think you've grown

00:12:43.590 --> 00:12:45.250
since I met you.

00:12:45.550 --> 00:12:48.200
You're like a little chick.

00:12:48.930 --> 00:12:51.130
You used to chirp as you walked.

00:12:48.980 --> 00:12:51.490
Chirp                             Chirp

00:12:51.490 --> 00:12:55.820
Chorp                               Chorp

00:12:51.610 --> 00:12:53.450
But now you "chorp."

00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:55.820
That sounds kinda gross!

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:59.810
And now, you're about to spread your wings!

00:13:01.100 --> 00:13:04.080
Shino, adult chickens still can't fly!

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:07.350
Oh, no!

00:13:07.980 --> 00:13:09.090
What's wrong, Aya?

00:13:09.610 --> 00:13:12.220
We haven't studied at all!

00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:19.740
Everything's so blurry, I can't see reality.

00:13:20.660 --> 00:13:22.140
I can't see.

00:13:22.140 --> 00:13:24.480
I can't see. I can't see.

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:31.160
So, how did it go?

00:13:29.730 --> 00:13:34.990
Not Bad

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:32.740
Awful!

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:38.990
Hello!!
Kin-iro Mosaic

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:43.040
Hello!!
Kin-iro Mosaic

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:48.040
I'll take the rag.

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:52.050
First Semester Closing Ceremony

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:51.080
Karen, you take the broom,
and Shino, you take the dustpan.

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:52.050
Yeah!

00:13:52.300 --> 00:13:54.830
I'm the batter, and Shino's the catcher!

00:13:53.580 --> 00:13:55.420
Let's do this!

00:13:57.050 --> 00:13:59.310
Start cleaning right now!

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:01.310
You have awful control!

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:05.770
Ayaya, do you like cleaning?

00:14:05.770 --> 00:14:07.510
I don't dislike it.

00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:08.730
Are you a clean freak?

00:14:08.730 --> 00:14:11.190
No, I'm normal.

00:14:11.670 --> 00:14:16.570
I heard that clean freaks
don't like to be touched.

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:19.250
What are you talking about?

00:14:21.580 --> 00:14:26.390
Darn it, Youko! You have to
clean your own classroom!

00:14:27.150 --> 00:14:28.330
What?

00:14:28.330 --> 00:14:30.250
Youko's special.

00:14:30.250 --> 00:14:31.520
Really?

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:39.680
Alice, what's wrong?

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:40.720
Youko...

00:14:41.350 --> 00:14:42.970
Look at this.

00:14:43.430 --> 00:14:44.660
What's this?

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:46.730
Is it burned?

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:48.410
Oh, it's a rag.

00:14:48.870 --> 00:14:51.980
Youko, no! Stop, Youko!

00:14:54.550 --> 00:14:57.710
Sorry. So what is this?

00:14:57.710 --> 00:14:58.740
Well, you see...

00:14:59.320 --> 00:15:02.790
When I was cleaning our room
with Shino the other day...

00:15:09.790 --> 00:15:12.110
I need to bring in the laundry.

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:13.880
I'll do it.

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:23.140
This is Shino's favorite handkerchief.

00:15:23.450 --> 00:15:26.900
I know! I'll iron it for her.

00:15:26.680 --> 00:15:27.590
Flag

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:35.980
Event

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:35.980
I knew you'd do that!

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:41.640
Alice, are you finished?

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:44.660
I-I'm done.

00:15:44.660 --> 00:15:47.860
Thanks to your hard work,
we finished up quickly.

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:49.940
Let's have a snack.

00:15:49.940 --> 00:15:52.190
<i>What should I do? I need to apologize!</i>

00:15:52.190 --> 00:15:54.800
<i>Now! Right now!</i>

00:15:55.560 --> 00:15:58.120
And now, here we are...

00:15:58.490 --> 00:16:02.110
Sh-Shouldn't you apologize
sooner rather than later?

00:16:02.110 --> 00:16:03.790
But now it's even dirtier.

00:16:03.790 --> 00:16:05.270
Sorry about that!

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:07.510
What's wrong, you two?

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:09.510
Kusshi-chan.

00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:13.070
I see.

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:16.880
Unfortunately, there's no way to mend this.

00:16:17.320 --> 00:16:19.140
You should apologize sincerely.

00:16:19.430 --> 00:16:20.460
But...

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:21.730
Ba-dump

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:24.990
It's okay! I'll go apologize with you!

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:31.660
Oomiya-san, I have something to tell you.

00:16:31.660 --> 00:16:33.240
Okay. What is it?

00:16:36.420 --> 00:16:38.400
I'm terribly sorry!

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:41.300
What? Please raise your heads!

00:16:45.170 --> 00:16:46.480
This handkerchief...

00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:50.090
I thought the wind blew it away.

00:16:50.090 --> 00:16:51.960
I-I'm sorry.

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:54.380
So that's why you were so down.

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:57.650
It's okay, Alice. Look at this.

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:01.450
It's shaped just like Australia.

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:02.770
Shino!

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:04.480
Alice.

00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:05.680
Shino!

00:17:05.680 --> 00:17:07.190
Alice.

00:17:08.810 --> 00:17:10.590
Shino!

00:17:12.220 --> 00:17:13.230
Alice.

00:17:13.230 --> 00:17:14.070
Shino!

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:15.690
<i>What?</i>

00:17:23.710 --> 00:17:27.030
<i>Karen-chan's hair is touching the floor.</i>

00:17:34.520 --> 00:17:36.580
<i>Blonde hair...</i>

00:17:39.220 --> 00:17:40.580
What are you doing?

00:17:45.150 --> 00:17:47.020
There we go...

00:17:47.020 --> 00:17:48.320
There we go.

00:17:48.320 --> 00:17:50.070
Youko!

00:17:50.800 --> 00:17:52.320
Hey, Aya.

00:17:55.440 --> 00:17:57.330
What are you doing?!

00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:02.880
Sheesh, you're so clumsy.

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:05.080
Well, you scared me.

00:18:05.650 --> 00:18:06.630
See you later.

00:18:06.630 --> 00:18:07.590
W-Wait!

00:18:07.970 --> 00:18:10.020
Why don't we play shiritori?

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:11.350
Okay...

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:12.980
Natsu (summer).

00:18:13.480 --> 00:18:15.020
Ts-Tsumiki (building blocks).

00:18:15.020 --> 00:18:16.100
Kitsutsuki (woodpecker).

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:17.410
Kinoko (mushroom).

00:18:17.410 --> 00:18:18.480
Koara (koala).

00:18:18.480 --> 00:18:19.610
Rappa (trumpet).

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:20.810
Parashuuto (parachute).

00:18:20.810 --> 00:18:24.060
To... to... to...

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:27.760
Well, see you later.

00:18:29.780 --> 00:18:31.050
Tokimeki (thrill)!

00:18:31.050 --> 00:18:32.580
Aya, the bell...

00:18:32.580 --> 00:18:35.490
It's your turn! The "ki" of "tokimeki"!

00:18:35.490 --> 00:18:36.990
What?!

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:48.500
Summer Vacation Notes
1. Follow the rules
2. Keep up with your studies
3. Don't get into any accidents

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:51.510
See you in the second semester!

00:18:48.950 --> 00:18:51.150
Summer vacation is finally here.

00:18:51.750 --> 00:18:53.450
It's summer vacation!

00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:55.130
Aren't you excited, Shino?

00:18:55.560 --> 00:18:57.100
Yes.

00:18:59.340 --> 00:19:02.140
We're going to buy swimsuits.

00:19:02.590 --> 00:19:04.540
What are you going to do, Karen and Youko?

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:08.230
I'm going to a restaurant
with my mom and dad.

00:19:08.530 --> 00:19:13.400
I promised to take Kouta and Mitsuki
home, so I'll pass this time.

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:17.610
I look forward to seeing your
new swimsuits at the beach.

00:19:17.610 --> 00:19:18.410
Yeah.

00:19:18.980 --> 00:19:21.280
I look forward to seeing you!

00:19:21.580 --> 00:19:23.910
Seeing you... Seeing you...

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:26.010
You're shameless, Youko!

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:27.080
Why?!

00:19:28.940 --> 00:19:30.600
See you later.

00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:32.310
Bye.

00:19:37.930 --> 00:19:40.290
It's so nice and cool in this store.

00:19:40.290 --> 00:19:41.680
It really is.

00:19:42.940 --> 00:19:45.120
What kind of swimsuit are you getting, Alice?

00:19:45.420 --> 00:19:48.560
Well, I actually drew a picture.

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:49.620
This is it.

00:19:51.200 --> 00:19:53.320
<i>What is that, a loincloth?</i>

00:19:54.830 --> 00:19:57.660
But maybe I'm not ready for a bikini.

00:19:57.660 --> 00:19:59.570
<i>What? That's a bikini?!</i>

00:19:59.570 --> 00:20:01.710
You're so mature, Alice.

00:20:01.710 --> 00:20:05.660
I'll go find an employee and ask if
they have anything like this here.

00:20:05.660 --> 00:20:06.780
Good idea.

00:20:06.780 --> 00:20:07.580
What?!

00:20:07.580 --> 00:20:10.760
<i>If she does that, they'll laugh at her!</i>

00:20:10.760 --> 00:20:11.590
Do...

00:20:11.590 --> 00:20:12.840
Dosukoi!

00:20:14.550 --> 00:20:15.470
Aya?

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:21.250
I-I'll pick out a swimsuit for you.

00:20:21.250 --> 00:20:22.820
Thanks!

00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:30.430
I'm glad you found a cute swimsuit.

00:20:30.430 --> 00:20:31.300
Yeah.

00:20:31.870 --> 00:20:33.840
I can't wait to wear it.

00:20:59.490 --> 00:21:03.880
Now all that's left is to
show Mom my report card...

00:21:10.300 --> 00:21:12.540
Shino, you have to accept reality!

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:15.530
Shino! Shino!

00:22:50.130 --> 00:22:53.060
Shinobu, let me see your report card.

00:22:55.000 --> 00:22:55.940
Here.

00:22:56.240 --> 00:22:57.380
Let's see.

00:22:59.660 --> 00:23:01.560
Oh, isn't this great?

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:02.990
Way to go.

00:23:05.550 --> 00:23:08.180
So where's yours?

00:23:06.180 --> 00:23:08.180
Class: 2-C, No. 2
Name: Alice Cartelet
Homeroom Teacher: Torimaru Sakura

00:23:10.630 --> 00:23:13.550
Please, I beg you! Let this one slide!

00:23:13.550 --> 00:23:16.190
Stop being stupid and show me!

00:23:16.930 --> 00:23:18.190
I'm sorry!

00:23:18.190 --> 00:23:19.310
<i>Shino...</i>

00:23:18.190 --> 00:23:19.820
Show me!

00:23:21.670 --> 00:23:23.510
Just how excited are you?!

00:23:23.510 --> 00:23:25.670
I was born in the summer, you know.

00:23:23.780 --> 00:23:25.280
Excited

00:23:25.670 --> 00:23:29.430
Summer's short, so we've
got to treasure each day!

00:23:29.280 --> 00:23:31.330
Giggle

00:23:29.330 --> 00:23:31.330
Yeah!

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:31.330
Youko-chan, you're like...

00:23:31.520 --> 00:23:32.730
a cicada!

00:23:32.730 --> 00:23:34.460
What kind of comparison is that?!

00:23:34.040 --> 00:23:36.040
#9     A Special Day

00:23:34.460 --> 00:23:35.260
Goodnight.

00:23:35.260 --> 00:23:36.040
See you later!
